### Fix 2: Reset the Action properly on Modal Close
Since we want the default selection to be *nothing* so the user is forced to think and click, we must ensure it resets to null when they close the modal.
**Find your handleCloseViewModal method (around line 430) and update setActionSelection:**
```javascript
  const handleCloseViewModal = () => {
    setIsViewModalOpen(false);
    setBatchDetails([]);
    setViewingBatchId(null);
    setViewingBatchCreatorId(null);
    setIsDescExpanded(false);

    // Reset Action UI states
    setIsActionMode(false);
    setActionSelection(null); // CHANGED: Reset to null so it forces user selection next time
    setExecutorRemarks("");
    setScheduleOverrideType("KEEP");
    setFinalScheduleTime("");
    fetchPendingBatches();
  };

```
